  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Cgi Federal obligated $109M in federal contracts in FY2027 to date. Cgi Federal won 41 awards so far, with an average award size of $2.7M. Cgi Federal's obligations fell 92.5% year over year. Historical context shows obligations of $1.1B in FY22, $1.1B in FY23, $1.2B in FY24, $1.2B in FY25, and $1.5B in FY26. The General Services Administration is the largest buyer in FY2027 to date, obligating $36.8M, followed by the Department of Health and Human Services with $31.9M and the Department of Justice with $24.3M. Computer Systems Design Services is the largest market, accounting for $68.3M of obligations, followed by Other Computer Related Services at $17.5M and Facilities Support Services at $15M. Smaller agency relationships include the Department of Veterans Affairs at $7.5M and the Department of Transportation at $7.2M. Several NAICS categories show minimal or zero obligations, including Engineering Services and Computer Facilities Management Services at $0.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How steep was the change in Cgi Federal's FY2027 obligations compared with prior years?",
        "body": "Cgi Federal's obligations in FY2027 to date are $109M. Cgi Federal's obligations fell 92.5% year over year. Prior fiscal years show much larger totals: $1.1B in FY22, $1.1B in FY23, $1.2B in FY24, $1.2B in FY25, and $1.5B in FY26. This places FY2027 to date well below the recent annual obligation levels."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies and markets drove Cgi Federal's FY2027 to date results?",
        "body": "The General Services Administration obligated $36.8M, the Department of Health and Human Services obligated $31.9M, and the Department of Justice obligated $24.3M. Computer Systems Design Services accounted for $68.3M, Other Computer Related Services accounted for $17.5M, and Facilities Support Services accounted for $15M. Smaller contributions include the Department of Veterans Affairs at $7.5M and the Department of Transportation at $7.2M."
      }
    ]
  },
